    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d745">

                <pb facs="0807" n="795" xml:id="pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/520a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-17T19:00:00-04:00">July 17, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>907. The Soviet Ambassador today asked if the American Government would be
                    willing to receive a Soviet military mission to the United States composed of
                    approximately six officers headed by Lieutenant-General Golikov.<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d745-f1"/> The purpose of this mission, the Ambassador said, would
                    be to supervise the placing of Soviet orders and to cooperate with the American
                    authorities in the procurement of supplies and equipment for the Soviet
                    Union.</p>
                <p>After discussing the matter with the President and the War Department, I have
                    informed the Ambassador that this Government would be pleased to receive such a
                    mission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d745-f1" n="40" xml:id="d745-f1-content">
                <p>This Soviet Military Mission arrived by airplane in New York on July 26, 1941.
                    Lt. Gen. Filip Ivanovich Golikov, Deputy Chief of Staff, was Chief of the
                    Mission: Division Engineer Alexander Konstantinovich Repin was Assistant Chief;
                    and 1st Lt. Nikolay Vasilyevich Evsikov was the Secretary.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
